WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.635
- Good morning Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.547
My one word is believe and I
believe that entrepreneurs will

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:08.077
solve all of the world's major problems.

00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:11.866
So to help on your journey,
today's message is shine.

00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:13.385
Over to you Tupac Shakur.

00:00:13.385 --> 00:00:15.766
(rooster crowing)

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:18.332
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:20.896
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:20.896 --> 00:00:24.396
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:28.326
- I can't explain why ...

00:00:28.326 --> 00:00:31.635
I shine and no one else shines.
I think everybody shines,

00:00:31.635 --> 00:00:34.572
in different things, and a
lot of things I can't do.

00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:36.488
I can't play basketball like every other

00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:38.188
black person in America,

00:00:38.188 --> 00:00:39.404
but I can act.

00:00:39.404 --> 00:00:41.993
I know how to go to
that true spot in myself

00:00:41.993 --> 00:00:43.639
'cuz I'm there every day.

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:46.946
I can be me. I can be whoever,
because I'm true to me.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.665
I can go to neutral easily.

00:00:48.665 --> 00:00:51.774
A lot of people, black,
white, Mexican, young or old,

00:00:51.774 --> 00:00:54.880
fat or skinny, have a problem
being true to they self.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.245
They have a problem looking in the mirror

00:00:56.245 --> 00:00:58.708
and looking directly into their own souls.

00:00:58.708 --> 00:01:00.488
The reason I sell six million records,

00:01:00.488 --> 00:01:02.857
the reason I can go to jail
and come out without a scratch,

00:01:02.857 --> 00:01:05.542
the reason I can walk around,
the reason I am who I am today

00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:07.876
is because I can look
directly into my face

00:01:07.876 --> 00:01:09.419
and find my soul, it's there.

00:01:09.419 --> 00:01:12.023
It's not sold. I didn't sell
it, it's there within me.

00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:15.259
I still feel it. My heart is
still connected to my body.

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:19.154
So I could, any character I'm a bring

00:01:19.154 --> 00:01:23.358
that intensity, that truth
and that honestly to it

00:01:23.358 --> 00:01:26.912
because I have to repay for that blessing,

00:01:26.912 --> 00:01:28.327
from black Jesus, from God.

00:01:28.327 --> 00:01:30.955
I have to pay for that, by shining.

00:01:30.955 --> 00:01:34.300
If he gives you the
voltage, and you waste it,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.421
that's the curse. He gave
me the voltage, I'm a shine.

00:01:37.421 --> 00:01:40.664
It's not mines, its from God. It's God.

00:01:40.664 --> 00:01:43.732
Not that its so special
that no body got it, but

00:01:43.732 --> 00:01:46.228
all of our gifts and blessings and,

00:01:46.228 --> 00:01:49.284
and our strengths and our
weaknesses come from God,

00:01:49.284 --> 00:01:51.866
come from black Jesus, or whoever,

00:01:51.866 --> 00:01:54.030
comes from within you. You know I mean?

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.276
So, it's not really
tricky, everybody can do it

00:01:57.276 --> 00:01:59.177
if they can just go to that spot.

00:01:59.177 --> 00:02:01.345
I guess all the things that
happened to me in my life

00:02:01.345 --> 00:02:02.825
allow me to go there easily.

00:02:02.825 --> 00:02:05.404
- I believe that everybody
has genius-level talent

00:02:05.404 --> 00:02:06.514
at something.

00:02:06.514 --> 00:02:11.124
Everybody, has genius-level
talent at something.

00:02:11.124 --> 00:02:12.981
People just don't know what it is.

00:02:12.981 --> 00:02:14.269
People just coast.

00:02:14.269 --> 00:02:16.930
They sit on their talent, or
they never even discover it.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.180
I can say that Michael Jordan
is not the greatest basketball

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.621
player of all time, that the
greatest basketball player of

00:02:21.621 --> 00:02:23.729
all time is the manager at Starbucks,

00:02:23.729 --> 00:02:27.300
because he didn't chase
his basketball dreams.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.519
Or because he never even
picked up a basketball.

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:32.725
Right? And so how many people
sit on their ambitions,

00:02:32.725 --> 00:02:34.933
sit on their dreams, sit on their desires,

00:02:34.933 --> 00:02:36.493
and don't actually take the action?

00:02:36.493 --> 00:02:39.825
You could have been Michael
Jordan in what you did,

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.527
but instead you're doing
this thing you're doing.

00:02:42.527 --> 00:02:43.360
That's most people.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.727
They wake up and they drive
to go work for somebody they

00:02:45.727 --> 00:02:49.210
don't like, in a job that
doesn't maximize their talents.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:51.758
They work with people who,
you know, don't respect them

00:02:51.758 --> 00:02:54.661
as much as they should, and
they do that every single day

00:02:54.661 --> 00:02:57.229
for the rest of their lives.
That's what most people

00:02:57.229 --> 00:02:58.976
wake up to do, and that's really sad.

00:02:58.976 --> 00:03:03.073
But it's no body else's
fault, besides your own.

00:03:03.073 --> 00:03:06.726
I believe it's your responsibility
to go and find the thing

00:03:06.726 --> 00:03:08.463
that you have genius-level talent at,

00:03:08.463 --> 00:03:09.638
that you can shine with.

00:03:09.638 --> 00:03:10.923
And some of you know it.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:13.644
Some of you know, like I can
be the best in the world,

00:03:13.644 --> 00:03:17.302
or among the best in the world at this.

00:03:17.302 --> 00:03:18.392
You know it.

00:03:18.392 --> 00:03:20.514
But you're just not taking
enough action on it.

00:03:20.514 --> 00:03:22.043
You're not committing
enough to it, you're not

00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:24.942
practicing hard enough to
get to where you want to go.

00:03:24.942 --> 00:03:27.130
Michael Jordan had
talent, but he practiced.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:29.634
He worked harder than anybody
on the Bulls, as well.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:32.781
You got to own your craft,
and practice and work it

00:03:32.781 --> 00:03:34.579
every single day.

00:03:34.579 --> 00:03:36.542
So some of you know what
you could have the potential

00:03:36.542 --> 00:03:38.857
to be great at, but you're
not putting in the work

00:03:38.857 --> 00:03:41.946
to get there. You're coasting.

00:03:41.946 --> 00:03:43.489
You've reached a certain
level, you're coasting 'cuz

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.196
its easy for you to do that
level, you don't have to

00:03:46.196 --> 00:03:48.577
put a lot of practice
and preparation into it.

00:03:48.577 --> 00:03:50.505
You know, you have other
responsibilities and so you're

00:03:50.505 --> 00:03:52.978
kind of coasting on this one
thing that you're talented at.

00:03:52.978 --> 00:03:55.042
Some of you don't even know it.

00:03:55.042 --> 00:03:56.662
Some of you have no idea
what you're talented at.

00:03:56.662 --> 00:03:58.735
You have no idea what your genius-level,

00:03:58.735 --> 00:04:01.272
Michael Jordan level, at.

00:04:01.272 --> 00:04:03.477
And so that's you that
you need to explore.

00:04:03.477 --> 00:04:05.691
Like that manager at Starbucks,
if he never picked up

00:04:05.691 --> 00:04:07.703
a basketball, he would never know

00:04:07.703 --> 00:04:09.451
he would be better than Michael Jordan.

00:04:09.451 --> 00:04:10.904
So you have to explore.
You have to say yes.

00:04:10.904 --> 00:04:12.515
You have to try things.

00:04:12.515 --> 00:04:15.630
If you have no idea what your
passion or your purpose is,

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.384
then say yes to almost anything.

00:04:18.384 --> 00:04:20.879
You know as long as its
legal, as long as it

00:04:20.879 --> 00:04:24.915
doesn't cause bodily harm.
There's a few criteria,

00:04:24.915 --> 00:04:26.864
but in general say yes to everything,

00:04:26.864 --> 00:04:29.158
and its something I
still try to adopt today.

00:04:29.158 --> 00:04:30.927
I say yes to new experiences.

00:04:30.927 --> 00:04:32.702
Say yes to trying out new things.

00:04:32.702 --> 00:04:36.526
Say yes to going to new countries.
Say yes to try new food.

00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:41.177
Say yes to going to new events.
Say yes, until you know.

00:04:41.177 --> 00:04:43.712
You know, you say yes to
trying that piece of sushi

00:04:43.712 --> 00:04:45.564
and you figure out I like sushi.

00:04:45.564 --> 00:04:47.358
Great we don't have to do that again.

00:04:47.358 --> 00:04:49.328
That's the definition of insanity, right?

00:04:49.328 --> 00:04:51.049
Its going back and doing the
same thing over and over again

00:04:51.049 --> 00:04:52.452
and expecting a different result.

00:04:52.452 --> 00:04:53.960
If you've tested it and then you know,

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.613
well I don't like rock
climbing. I don't like the thing

00:04:56.613 --> 00:05:00.537
in my crotch. I don't
like heights. I tried it.

00:05:00.537 --> 00:05:03.848
I said yes, I tried it
... I didn't like it.

00:05:03.848 --> 00:05:06.301
Great, I don't have to go do it again.

00:05:06.301 --> 00:05:08.683
But if you don't know what
it is that you love to do,

00:05:08.683 --> 00:05:11.537
then you have to try. You say
yes, you say yes, you say yes,

00:05:11.537 --> 00:05:13.960
until you find the thing that
makes you come alive that you

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.240
want to do over and over and
over and over and over again,

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.998
until you shine.

00:05:18.998 --> 00:05:21.378
You have Michael Jordan
level talent in something,

00:05:21.378 --> 00:05:23.446
and it desperately wants you to find it

00:05:23.446 --> 00:05:25.629
and act on it, to make a positive impact,

00:05:25.629 --> 00:05:27.674
not just for yourself, but your community,

00:05:27.674 --> 00:05:29.595
the people around you, your family,

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:30.648
and the world.

00:05:30.648 --> 00:05:34.044
So the question of the day today
is, I'm curious, two parts.

00:05:34.044 --> 00:05:35.461
One, do you know,

00:05:36.325 --> 00:05:39.706
what you have Michael
Jordan level talent at?

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:42.152
And two, if you do, what is it?

00:05:42.152 --> 00:05:45.197
Both yes or no question and the answer,

00:05:45.197 --> 00:05:47.459
leave in the comments below.
I'm real excited to find out.

00:05:47.459 --> 00:05:49.534
I also want to give a
quick shout-out to Mzi Tom.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:51.271
Thank you so much for picking up a copy

00:05:51.271 --> 00:05:54.557
of my book Your One Word. I
really appreciate the support

00:05:54.557 --> 00:05:56.532
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:05:56.532 --> 00:05:58.094
So thank you guys so much for watching,

00:05:58.094 --> 00:06:01.252
I believe in you. I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:06:01.252 --> 00:06:04.793
and whatever your one word
is, much love and I'll see you

00:06:04.793 --> 00:06:08.924
again tomorrow morning for
another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:08.924 --> 00:06:11.525
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:11.525 --> 00:06:15.092
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:06:15.092 --> 00:06:17.943
(typewriter clicking)

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.167
- You know my mother used to tell me,

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:21.139
"Todd, you can do anything
you put your mind to."

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:23.705
And my grandmother used to tell me,

00:06:23.705 --> 00:06:26.263
"If a task is once begun,
never leave it til its done.

00:06:26.263 --> 00:06:29.560
"Be the labor great or small,
do it well or not at all."

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:32.128
And I kind of grew up with
that mantra, you know?

00:06:32.128 --> 00:06:33.642
- I grew up believing that

00:06:33.642 --> 00:06:37.110
you could do anything you
put your mind to, you know?

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:38.360
And I don't ...

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:44.393
No matter what, you know,
I am extremely determined.

00:06:44.393 --> 00:06:45.816
- Like I'm like, abnormally--

00:06:45.816 --> 00:06:49.676
- Its like that need to
succeed, never goes away, right?

00:06:49.676 --> 00:06:53.593
- It's not only, it's
not just a general like--

00:06:54.851 --> 00:06:55.684
succeed--
- [TT] It's that fire.

00:06:55.684 --> 00:06:58.805
- for the success, for
the sake of succeeding,

00:06:58.805 --> 00:07:01.480
its a desire to create.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.313
- [TT] Yeah.
- You know I'm saying?

00:07:02.313 --> 00:07:06.477
To use the Godly power and
talent that was instilled in me

00:07:06.477 --> 00:07:09.916
to the best of my ability,
to maximize my potential.

00:07:09.916 --> 00:07:12.447
Because if I'm not here
to maximize my potential,

00:07:12.447 --> 00:07:13.696
then what am I on earth for?

00:07:13.696 --> 00:07:15.620
- Well my message to the
youth pretty much man,

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.384
is just to follow your
dreams, you know what I mean?

00:07:17.384 --> 00:07:21.946
I think a lot of people get
caught up and get sidetracked

00:07:21.946 --> 00:07:24.677
by what's happening around
them, and what's cool.

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:27.155
People always ignore they
gift, no realizing that gift

00:07:27.155 --> 00:07:28.735
is what's going to take
you out of your poverty,

00:07:28.735 --> 00:07:30.232
take you out of your situation.

00:07:30.232 --> 00:07:34.659
That gift is the ultimate
element that God provided for you

00:07:34.659 --> 00:07:37.618
to get you out of any situation,
or to take you to what

00:07:37.618 --> 00:07:40.104
destined for you. You, know,
some people are just great at

00:07:40.104 --> 00:07:43.883
certain things, but
because music, or modeling,

00:07:43.883 --> 00:07:47.281
or film is cool, they
alienate what their gifts are

00:07:47.281 --> 00:07:50.804
just to be a part of something
that is pursued to be,

00:07:50.804 --> 00:07:52.452
or persuaded to be cool.

00:07:52.452 --> 00:07:54.534
So I always felt like, you know, my method

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:55.979
and message always has been,

00:07:55.979 --> 00:07:57.943
to just follow the gift that you have,

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.508
put a lot of emphasize in it.

00:07:59.508 --> 00:08:01.707
Concentrate on what you
feel that you're great in,

00:08:01.707 --> 00:08:02.595
because what you're great in,

00:08:02.595 --> 00:08:04.503
is always going to be what pulls you out

00:08:04.503 --> 00:08:06.602
of the worst situations
that you could ever imagine,

00:08:06.602 --> 00:08:09.166
and put you in a better
situation, like being in debt.

00:08:09.166 --> 00:08:12.955
When you fully accept that
you are here to be great,

00:08:12.955 --> 00:08:15.924
when you fully accept that
you are here to be happy,

00:08:15.924 --> 00:08:18.752
when you fully accept that
you're here to receive,

00:08:18.752 --> 00:08:22.002
when you fully accept that you can have

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.468
the peace and the serenity,
and the joy and the wisdom,

00:08:25.468 --> 00:08:27.518
and the purpose and the intention

00:08:27.518 --> 00:08:29.350
that you intend to bring to the world,

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:32.350
and that it is all available to you.

00:08:33.186 --> 00:08:36.801
That's is when life gets very groovy.

00:08:36.801 --> 00:08:40.193
And so my hope and my intention for today,

00:08:40.193 --> 00:08:44.215
is to wake you up to that
presence and more importantly,

00:08:44.215 --> 00:08:47.520
give you a really great New
York City kick in the ass that

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:51.528
says not only I'm awake to it,
not only do I believe in it,

00:08:51.528 --> 00:08:53.611
but I am committed to it.

00:08:54.871 --> 00:08:59.547
I am unapologetic about
my capacity to be great.

00:08:59.547 --> 00:09:02.553
I am unapologetic about
my capacity to heal.

00:09:02.553 --> 00:09:05.066
I am unapologetic about my capacity to see

00:09:05.066 --> 00:09:06.613
beyond my physical sight.

00:09:06.613 --> 00:09:09.629
I am unapologetic about my capacity to

00:09:09.629 --> 00:09:12.131
shine as bright as I can shine,

00:09:12.131 --> 00:09:15.373
because I trust and I know
that when I shine bright,

00:09:15.373 --> 00:09:18.605
I give others permission to do the same

00:09:18.605 --> 00:09:21.272
and in my glow they wake up too,

00:09:22.516 --> 00:09:23.349
and that

00:09:24.517 --> 00:09:26.017
is why we're here.

